---
layout: layouts/admin.njk
adminPage: website
pagination:
  data: consoleNav.website
  size: 1
  alias: tab
eleventyComputed:
  permalink: "{{ tab.url }}index.html"
  websiteTab: "{{ tab.tab }}"
  adminTitle: "{{ tab.label }}"
  adminHeading: "{{ tab.heading | safe }}"
  headingKey: "{{ tab.page }}"
---
{#- THE WEBSITE AREA, ONE PAGE (Chase, 2026-09-27): every tab is here, and
   every tab's data loads when the page does — so moving between tabs is
   instant, and an unsaved edit on one tab is still there after a look at
   another. Written at each tab's own address, opening on that tab, so a
   reload or a bookmark returns to where you were; admin-website.js moves
   between them without a reload and keeps the address in step.

   Each tab's markup is its own include (src/_includes/website/), unchanged
   from when it was a page of its own, and each tab's script finds its own
   elements, so the five do not know about one another — except for one
   thing, the site settings they share: see admin-website.js. -#}
{%- for t in consoleNav.website %}
<section class="web-panel" data-web-panel="{{ t.tab }}"{% if t.tab != websiteTab %} hidden{% endif %}>
  {% include "website/" + t.tab + ".njk" %}
</section>
{%- endfor %}

{#- The languages this build publishes, for Resources and Events: the same list
   Eleventy paginated the public pages over, so the editor cannot offer a
   language the site does not render. -#}
<script id="libLangs" type="application/json">{{ activeLangs | dump | safe }}</script>
